ees Certificate Programs Majors Athletics A-Z Index Info For Alumni Students Faculty Staff Parents Community Apply Visit Give Close Home PLACE PLACE Section Menu PLACE Students Alumni Faculty/Staff Parents, Friends, & Family Community Partners On-Campus Student Employment Events, Workshops, & Special Programs Handshake Find your strengths PLACE is our on-campus career center dedicated to helping students discover their place through Purpose, Life And Career Exploration. With guidance from our expert staff, students can explore their interests, map out next steps and tap into personalized support as they prepare for life after graduation. Get started today! Set up a profile in Handshake, Roanoke College's career platform, to access resources and schedule appointments for career advising. Appointments are available in-person, virtually or via phone. Instructions Handshake Services One-on-One Advising: Personalized guidance to help you pursue purpose on campus and in life beyond. Connections: Access to current jobs, internships, and meaningful experiences. Alumni Access: Networking opportunities with RC Grads for mentorships and career connections. Document Development: Guidance drafting a wide variety of professional documents, including resumes and cover letters. Continuing Education: Assistance searching for and applying to graduate school, licensure programs, or specialized training. Professional Coaching: Support to help students define and execute personal and professional career goals while further developing general employability skills. Experiences: Assistance finding on-campus employment opportunities to help students gain valuable work skills and confidence, while becoming an important part of the campus community. Career Planning Guide: Unlock your full potential and shape your future with our comprehensive career planning guide , designed to empower your journey towards a fulfilling and impactful career. How PLACE Helps Students Junior International Relations and Religious Studies major Abby talks about Roanoke's PLACE (Purpose, Life and Career Exploration) and its role in her career development, her achievements such as internships and work in gender health, and how PLACE assists students in finding their post-graduation purpose. News 2026 Summer Internship Roundup From growing vegetables in the campus garden to working with patients in the operating room, our students had some pretty incredible internships over the summer. Roanoke College joins Google AI for Education Accelerator Through the program, students, faculty and staff will have access to artificial intelligence training and Google Career Certificates at no cost. Contact Us PLACE Department: PLACE Phone: 540-375-2303 Fax: 540-375-2092 MailingAddress: 202 Maxey Way Salem, Virginia 24153 Location: Fowler House Email: place@roanoke.edu PLACE LinkedIn Group PLACE Students Alumni Faculty/Staff Parents, Friends, & Family Community Partners On-Campus Student Employment Events, Workshops, & Special Programs Handshake Find your strengths 221 College Lane, Salem, Virginia 24153 540-375-2500 (Main Telephone Number) Contact Us Maps & Parking Roanoke on Social © 2026 Roanoke College. All rights reserved. Roanoke College, Elderscholar, The Management Institute, Roanoke Review, Roanoke Maroons and associated logos are trademarks of Roanoke College. Policies Careers at Roanoke College Operating Status Legal Notices × Notice We  (www.roanoke.edu)   and selected third parties  (10)   collect personal information as specified in the privacy policy . You can give or deny your consent to the processing of your precise geolocation data at any time via the “Accept all” and “Reject all” buttons or inside the privacy choices panel . Sale of my personal information Sharing of my personal information Processing of my personal information for targeted advertising Processing of my precise geolocation data Press again to continue 0/1 Learn more Reject all Save and continue"
