ement shifts in The Cavern. Education, Experience, Skills, and Abilities: • 2+ years of foodservice or hospitality supervisory management experience is required. • Preference given to candidates with an associate’s degree (or higher) in Hospitality, Tourism, Business Management, or similar field. • Previous experience in high-volume, fast-paced college and university dining is preferred. Proficient computer skills, including Microsoft Office, vendor online order systems, point-of-sale systems, timekeeping systems, recipe and inventory database management, and inventory management. • Projects a positive, professional image. Maintains a high level of competence, good judgment, discretion, confidentiality, and sound decision-making skills. • Ability to meticulously maintain a clean and safe food service environment Special Conditions of Employment: • Satisfactory conviction history background check. • Must be legally eligible to open, dispense, serve, and transport alcohol-containing beverages in the state of Virginia • Maintain a valid VA driver’s license, a clean DMV record and successful completion (and annual renewal) of required Roanoke College driver training programs. • Must have current certification or be able to pass ServSafe Manager and Food Allergy Research & Education (FARE) certification exams within 6 months of employment and renew as needed. • Dining services staff are considered essential personnel. In the event of a university closure, modification, or suspension due to weather or other emergency conditions, this position is expected to make all reasonable attempts to report to work as scheduled for the duration of the closure/suspension. • Attend trade shows, conferences, and off-site training as required. • Availability to work flexible hours, including early mornings or late nights, evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed to accommodate operational needs. Return to Roanoke College Apply for this job Apply for this job Apply for this job SHARE No