      "description": "Electrician  job at Roanoke College  in Salem, VA, powered by JobScore Your browser cookies must be enabled in order to apply for this job. Please contact support@jobscore.com if you need further instruction on how to do that. Electrician Physical Plant | Salem, VA | Full Time | Opened almost 3 years ago | From $22.00 to $28.00 per hour ‹ › Job Description About Roanoke College Roanoke College is a place where every student who works hard has the opportunity to succeed. We champion potential, providing essential learning and leadership through innovative academic programs and transformative educational experiences, giving students the mettle, mindset, and empathy to pursue lives of purpose, build meaningful careers, and meet society’s most pressing needs. Located in scenic Salem, Virginia, Roanoke College is an intimate, welcoming community that has served the local region and beyond for nearly 200 years. Now, we’re building on momentum and offering a Roanoke experience for today’s students and a legacy that belongs to every Maroon. Learn about the College's new strategic plan, Imagine Roanoke: A Strategic Plan for Roanoke College and the 21st Century Learner . Roanoke College is a nationally ranked residential liberal arts college affiliated with the Lutheran Church (ELCA), located in the beautiful Roanoke Valley of Virginia. A Phi Beta Kappa institution, Roanoke College is an equal opportunity employer and actively seeks diversity among its faculty, staff, and students; women and members of under-represented groups are especially encouraged to apply. The Position At Roanoke College, we are committed to creating a safe and productive environment for our students and staff. We are currently seeking a motivated electrical helper to join our campus facilities team and assist in maintaining and improving our electrical systems. You will have the opportunity to work with experienced electricians and contribute to the efficient operation of electrical systems throughout the college. Roanoke College provides uniforms, tools, safety equipment, and lunch each day. This position is eligible for full college benefits and works a core schedule of 7:30 a.m. to 4 p.m., Monday – Friday. Key Responsibilities : Assisting with electrical installations, repairs, and maintenance. Helping in diagnosing electrical problems and participating in troubleshooting. Assisting with routine inspections and electrical system checks. Safely and effectively using tools and equipment. Learning and following electrical codes and standards. Maintaining accurate records of work performed. Assist in setting up and maintaining electrical systems. Support the installation and maintenance of lighting, wiring, and electrical devices. Help with safety checks and inspections of electrical equipment. Participate in electrical projects, including wiring and panel installations. Work collaboratively with the team to ensure work is performed efficiently and safely. Education, Experience, Skills, and Abilities : Basic knowledge of electrical systems A strong work ethic, a desire to learn, and the ability to follow directions. Good physical condition to perform tasks that may require lifting and working in various conditions. Reliable, punctual, and safety-conscious. Strong communication and teamwork skills. A valid Virginia driver's license and near clean driving record. Ability to pass a criminal background check. Ability to work some evenings and weekends for on call rotations. Return to Roanoke College Apply for this job Apply for this job Apply for this job SHARE Not the right job? Join our Talent Network Location Return to Roanoke College POWERED BY APPLICANT TRACKING"
    },
