ge (forced and gravity) Accomplishes assigned and scheduled maintenance programs in accordance with established directives and procedures. Maintain, service, and repair hydraulic, air, gas, distilled water and steam lines and HVAC lines. Renders services involved as a result of repair, alteration, modification, rehabilitation and minor new construction accomplished on campus buildings, fixtures and structures. Assists the Manager of Physical Plant in the preparation of work estimates involving plumbing and steam fitting; shop for purchase materials necessary for his branch; provide the Manager of Physical Plant with requirements for materials and equipment not locally available; maintain and submit to his supervisor records of materials and time used on work orders. Supports other trades as required. Reports any unsafe conditions pertaining to building plumbing, steam, condensate or other plumbing systems and makes recommendations for proper repair. Perform other duties as assigned. Education, Experience, Skills, and Abilities : Journeyman license Five or more year’s commercial plumbing experience Backflow certification preferred Ability to work in a team Return to Roanoke College Apply for this job Apply for this job Apply for this job SHARE Not the right job? Join our Talent Network Location Return to Roanoke College POWERED BY APPLICANT TRACKING"
